(Regression test: assigning or initializing a buffer with a number -
literal or number variable - used to print a garbage pointer address
instead of the number's text. Both the buffer VarDecl initializer path
and the Assignment path generated the value into rax and THEN called
_buffer_clear, which returns the cleared buffer's new pointer in rax,
clobbering the value; the subsequent formatted-int append then read
that pointer as the value to format. The fix clears the buffer before
materializing the value.)

a buffer called "b1" is 5.
Print b1.
a number called "n" is 42.
a buffer called "b2" is n.
Print b2.
a buffer called "b3" is 32 bytes in size.
b3 is 7.
b3 is 123.
Print b3.
b3 is n.
Print b3.
